            // In pre state (Collecting): combiner_has(i) means i < elems.len() && elems[i].is_Some()
            // In post state (Responding with idx=0): combiner_has(i) means i >= 0 && elems[i].is_Some()
            // Since i >= 0 is always true for nat, and in pre state valid_idx(i) implies i < num_clients
            // and elems.len() == num_clients (from preconditions), we have i < elems.len() == i >= 0 for valid indices

